WEBVTT

00:00.960 --> 00:03.330
It's absurd that Ratt should vanish
because of me coming here!

00:04.330 --> 00:06.870
The wind is blowing, Noah.

00:06.870 --> 00:08.600
I will punish you!

00:08.600 --> 00:12.630
Your country's heartless " ideals" don't
mean a damn thing to me!

00:19.410 --> 00:23.480
If you survive, I know you'll make it back to Calm.

00:23.890 --> 00:26.180
Farewell, Noah.

00:30.890 --> 00:38.630
We've all surely got our arms outstretched

00:38.630 --> 00:45.600
Towards a far, faraway place

00:58.950 --> 01:05.160
Blown by the wind, we walk on

01:05.160 --> 01:12.120
Wanting to know the reason we were born

01:12.330 --> 01:18.640
Even if a time of loss should come

01:18.640 --> 01:25.770
Let's now choose to hold each other tight

01:28.220 --> 01:35.620
We've all surely got our arms outstretched

01:35.620 --> 01:41.600
Towards something we can't lose

01:41.600 --> 01:49.240
Pulling only brilliant dreams closer

01:49.240 --> 01:56.110
Towards a far, faraway place

02:01.720 --> 02:05.450
Episode 7
Awakened Feelings

02:12.430 --> 02:15.760
Oh, that Master Robès, he moves so brilliantly!

02:15.760 --> 02:18.290
Keep an eye on what your
opponent is doing, Zed!

02:19.500 --> 02:21.130
Zed!

02:24.570 --> 02:26.540
The difference in strength here is evident.

02:26.540 --> 02:30.040
Why would Robès accept a match such as this?

02:30.040 --> 02:35.510
He is merely fascinated by the
boy's hidden power.

02:36.280 --> 02:40.520
They polish their technique by fighting each
other and thereby improve their skills.

02:40.520 --> 02:43.990
That, in essence, is what the Joust is all about.

02:43.990 --> 02:46.890
The tradition and prestige that go with
it are of lesser importance.

02:56.800 --> 02:59.040
Damn, why won't it come out?

02:59.040 --> 03:01.670
How can I get it to come out when I want it to?

03:06.750 --> 03:08.550
Such a bore...

03:17.890 --> 03:21.850
I shall not make use of a single
shard during this match!

03:24.070 --> 03:27.930
Furthermore, I guarantee that I shall
triumph in glorious fashion.

03:32.440 --> 03:36.340
Well, now, I think that should
liven things up a bit.

03:36.340 --> 03:39.310
Go ahead and attack me as you please.

03:39.310 --> 03:41.280
Don't screw with me!

03:49.890 --> 03:52.330
You son of a bitch, you better
stop screwing with me!

03:52.330 --> 03:54.560
This is all your fault.

03:54.560 --> 03:58.400
I want to face off against your spirit.

03:58.400 --> 04:03.400
I want to demonstrate before all of these people
whether or not it is stronger than Belladonna.

04:03.400 --> 04:07.810
But it turns out you can't call out
your spirit, much less control it.

04:07.810 --> 04:12.950
So, I've merely devised a means to make this
boring match at least somewhat more enjoyable.

04:12.950 --> 04:15.280
Enough of this crap!

04:44.780 --> 04:46.180
What's the matter?

04:46.180 --> 04:50.590
Weren't you going to triumph in glorious fashion,
without using a single shard?

04:50.590 --> 04:55.490
Well, not like I'd ever trust what a
lowdown dirty thief says anyway!

04:55.490 --> 04:57.460
Here I come, Robès!

05:03.000 --> 05:04.970
He said he wouldn't use his spirit!

05:08.500 --> 05:09.970
Robès, you...

05:17.450 --> 05:18.710
What the hell?

05:18.710 --> 05:20.680
Why won't you do what I say?!

05:44.070 --> 05:46.170
Th..The winner: Robès!

05:46.170 --> 05:47.800
Zed!

05:49.610 --> 05:51.240
Zed!

06:07.530 --> 06:09.060
Well, there we have it.

06:09.060 --> 06:14.470
It seems the boy has not yet claimed
the spirit's power as his own.

06:17.240 --> 06:18.170
Zed?

06:18.170 --> 06:19.640
Zed?
Zed?

06:24.380 --> 06:27.840
I see, I lost, huh?

06:28.820 --> 06:30.440
Zed...

06:31.150 --> 06:34.460
Well, it was crazy for you to take on
Master Robès in the first place!

06:34.460 --> 06:36.460
But you did awesome!

06:36.460 --> 06:38.520
I thought you put up a great fight.

06:40.060 --> 06:41.560
You'll be all right now.

06:41.560 --> 06:43.460
I gave you first aid.

06:43.460 --> 06:46.090
Now, just see that you get some good rest.

06:51.570 --> 06:55.140
Robès, that was an excellent fight.

06:55.140 --> 07:00.150
I formally acknowledge you as
this year's shard champion.

07:00.150 --> 07:04.390
This is a chaotic era, with all countries
fighting for supremacy.

07:04.390 --> 07:09.220
You will no doubt serve as a great
inspiration to all shard casters.

07:09.220 --> 07:12.520
Shucks, if only Teacher hadn't been injured.

07:13.560 --> 07:15.620
Nothing we can do now.

07:24.740 --> 07:26.310
Oh, Dumas!

07:26.310 --> 07:27.610
Elder?

07:27.610 --> 07:29.510
Are you feeling all right now?

07:29.510 --> 07:32.040
Yes, you needn't worry about me.

07:32.780 --> 07:34.850
It is a pity, though.

07:34.850 --> 07:38.690
I had thought you would win again this year.

07:38.690 --> 07:40.460
There are times

07:40.460 --> 07:43.320
when the a outcome of a duel is more a matter
of luck than an individual's strength.

07:43.930 --> 07:45.720
If you'll excuse me...

07:51.770 --> 07:54.500
Oh! What is it, boy?

07:57.770 --> 08:00.610
You're looking rather meek.

08:00.610 --> 08:02.580
What am I supposed to do?

08:05.710 --> 08:07.320
I want...

08:07.320 --> 08:09.840
I want to become stronger.

08:12.120 --> 08:15.210
I want to become stronger! Stronger!

08:19.890 --> 08:23.090
I believe I told you to learn from Dumas.

08:32.010 --> 08:33.740
Dumas...

08:49.860 --> 08:54.450
Zymot Headquarters

09:00.970 --> 09:04.110
Hey, Elmeida, that's a new kind of spirit, isn't it?

09:04.110 --> 09:06.600
Who cares about those small fries?

09:08.580 --> 09:11.640
More importantly, when is this
match going to be over?

09:29.300 --> 09:31.090
Excellent work.

09:32.300 --> 09:34.370
That was a splendid match.

09:34.370 --> 09:40.030
Those who win Zymot's Joust receive the
opportunity to challenge one of us.

09:40.740 --> 09:42.710
Go ahead, choose.

09:47.950 --> 09:49.380
C'mon, what's the matter?

09:49.380 --> 09:53.020
You can become one of the three
top officials if you win!

09:53.020 --> 09:55.420
Go on and choose one of us!

09:55.420 --> 09:58.190
Then I choose you, Master Glaudio!

09:58.190 --> 10:00.290
Did you hear that? He said me!

10:00.290 --> 10:02.090
All right!

10:39.000 --> 10:41.870
Aw, heck, he wasn't so great.

10:43.040 --> 10:44.170
I leave the rest to you.

10:44.170 --> 10:45.170
Hey...

10:45.170 --> 10:47.900
So, when do we launch our operation?

10:48.310 --> 10:51.750
As soon as we receive word from the Joker.

10:51.750 --> 10:56.950
Yeah? Well, just don't forget that
Neotopia's on the move now.

10:59.220 --> 11:01.850
Not a problem, I've taken all things into account.

11:03.620 --> 11:06.490
Including the moves those Tuskans are making.

11:11.830 --> 11:14.100
What did you think, Lady Despara?

11:14.100 --> 11:17.670
The momentous Joust, held by
the new government...

11:17.670 --> 11:19.740
I enjoyed myself.

11:19.740 --> 11:21.240
By the way...

11:21.240 --> 11:26.050
Are the rumors true that the princess from
the previous ruling family lives?

11:26.050 --> 11:27.480
Who ever said such a thing?

11:27.480 --> 11:31.440
That is pure gossip, nonsense fabricated
by the resistance movement!

12:21.500 --> 12:23.400
Master Robès?

12:23.400 --> 12:25.770
Ah, it's you, enter.

12:27.070 --> 12:29.010
Master Khan has arrived.

12:29.010 --> 12:32.070
There is a pressing matter he wishes
to speak to you about.

12:32.480 --> 12:33.780
Khan, you say?

12:33.780 --> 12:36.650
Send him away! I have no interest
in stuffy people like him.

12:36.650 --> 12:39.280
But, sir, he's been waiting an hour already!

12:39.990 --> 12:41.780
Master Robès?

12:42.890 --> 12:44.760
All right...

12:44.760 --> 12:46.830
But I will have my bath first.

12:46.830 --> 12:48.620
Yes, sir...

12:50.300 --> 12:53.730
Master Robès! Please give up your thievery!

12:53.730 --> 12:56.470
If you are ever exposed, your future,
all your fortune, your family,

12:56.470 --> 12:58.810
which is already facing financial
difficulty, will be ruined!

12:58.810 --> 13:01.280
It's okay, this is just some fun to pass the time.

13:01.280 --> 13:02.940
But, sir!

13:02.940 --> 13:05.570
There is no way I'll be caught, is there?

13:09.850 --> 13:11.820
What did you just say?

13:12.850 --> 13:15.690
I want you to capture the mysterious
master thief, No-Face.

13:22.430 --> 13:23.630
What is so funny?

13:23.630 --> 13:28.100
Do pardon me, but I find it a most interesting
plan for you to have come up with.

13:28.100 --> 13:30.400
This is the decision of the Council.

13:30.400 --> 13:34.340
We believe that No-Face may
be a Zymotan Joker.

13:34.340 --> 13:37.210
What to do...

13:37.210 --> 13:41.480
I believe it is also a chance for you to command
recognition as a true champion.

13:45.290 --> 13:47.250
Wouldn't you agree?

13:50.690 --> 13:52.060
Very well!

13:52.060 --> 13:56.020
Then first, let's put a price on No-Face,
in order to solicit assistance.

13:56.430 --> 14:00.230
Given the current circumstances, we won't
be able to appropriate funds.

14:00.230 --> 14:04.800
Worry not, for the noble House of Redondo
shall shoulder the expense.

15:33.130 --> 15:35.230
Lunch is ready, guys!

15:35.230 --> 15:38.430
Okay! Am I hungry!

15:43.700 --> 15:45.330
Say...

15:47.570 --> 15:50.240
I entered the Joust in your place.

15:52.580 --> 15:54.550
Sorry for losing.

15:57.380 --> 15:59.120
Don't worry about it.

15:59.120 --> 16:01.060
Winning or losing is the luck of the draw.

16:01.060 --> 16:03.220
What matters most is what lies ahead.

16:16.900 --> 16:18.870
Don't let him get away!

16:23.080 --> 16:25.940
Well, here they are, bounty-hunting dogs.

16:31.350 --> 16:32.450
Give me more...

16:32.450 --> 16:34.420
Give me more enjoyment!

16:36.390 --> 16:41.630
Master Robès! Why will you
not give up this thievery?

16:41.630 --> 16:44.260
If you continue like this, it will bring
ruin upon the House of Redondo;

16:44.260 --> 16:46.500
you'll not be able to face your noble ancestors!

16:46.500 --> 16:51.300
What's more, if anything were
to happen to you, I... I...

16:51.940 --> 16:54.570
All right, only once more.

16:56.310 --> 16:57.950
Only once more?

16:57.950 --> 17:02.550
Yes, one more time, in order
to settle things properly.

17:02.550 --> 17:03.720
And you know what?

17:03.720 --> 17:06.350
I will need your assistance.

17:16.400 --> 17:20.700
Say, will I really become able to control
spirits just by doing this?

17:21.740 --> 17:24.470
Harmony with the land...

17:24.470 --> 17:26.770
Being in harmony with the land

17:26.770 --> 17:31.110
means you've mastered the spiritual power
to be able to accept things as they are.

17:31.110 --> 17:34.880
That is an important state to achieve
if you're to control spirits.

17:34.880 --> 17:37.010
Don't try to rush everything.

17:39.650 --> 17:41.620
Mr. Dumas!

17:45.490 --> 17:47.460
What's the matter?

17:53.900 --> 17:56.140
What are you guys doing?

17:56.140 --> 17:57.910
It's not our move-out deadline yet!

17:57.910 --> 17:59.910
What's the meaning of this?

17:59.910 --> 18:01.410
Say what you want,

18:01.410 --> 18:05.350
but we got orders from the House of Redondo
to clear all this away by the end of the day.

18:05.350 --> 18:06.350
House of Redondo?

18:06.350 --> 18:09.350
Hey, if you got a problem, then
take it straight to them.

18:09.350 --> 18:11.150
No way... Teacher?

18:11.150 --> 18:14.250
This land has been leased from
the House of Redondo.

18:14.860 --> 18:16.880
There's nothing we can do about this.

18:20.490 --> 18:21.560
I have an idea!

18:21.560 --> 18:25.230
Did you know there's a bounty out
for the capture of No-Face?

18:25.230 --> 18:26.930
I'm sure you'd be able to catch him easily!

18:26.930 --> 18:28.900
There is no need for that.

18:31.310 --> 18:33.710
The House of Redondo,
that's Robès's family, isn't it?

18:34.410 --> 18:36.540
Well, yeah, but...

18:36.540 --> 18:38.510
Don't tell me you...

18:41.950 --> 18:45.190
Yeah, I'll catch him.

18:45.190 --> 18:47.220
I swear I'll catch him and pay him back!

18:47.220 --> 18:49.550
What are you talking about?
What's that supposed to mean?!

19:00.030 --> 19:03.500
I never expected you to enter
the Joust competition!

19:03.500 --> 19:05.870
Yes, we were truly surprised!

19:06.470 --> 19:08.810
And you won the championship no less!

19:08.810 --> 19:10.340
Most impressive, Master Robès.

19:10.340 --> 19:12.840
I'm finding myself more a fan of yours than ever!

19:13.680 --> 19:15.050
You are too kind.

19:15.050 --> 19:18.550
A true championship would have been
mine by defeating Dumas.

19:18.550 --> 19:21.990
There is no meaning in having beaten
a child like the one I fought.

19:21.990 --> 19:26.130
I'm afraid I owe you my sincerest apologies for
the boring match you had to sit through.

19:26.130 --> 19:28.330
No, it was nothing of the sort!
Not at all! It was nothing of the sort!

19:28.330 --> 19:29.960
Robès!

19:34.270 --> 19:36.200
Why, if it isn't Zed!

19:36.200 --> 19:38.210
I do not recall inviting you, however.

19:38.210 --> 19:40.710
Nah, I'm not here for the party.

19:40.710 --> 19:43.580
I came here to kick your ass, No-Face!

19:43.580 --> 19:45.780
What a thing to say!

19:45.780 --> 19:47.750
That's downright rude!

19:48.150 --> 19:50.920
Here, c'mon, let's head home quick, okay?

19:50.920 --> 19:52.950
Make no mistake, he's the one for sure.

19:52.950 --> 19:55.690
M..Master Robès, I have terrible news!

19:55.690 --> 19:58.890
The mysterious master thief,
No-Face has appeared!

20:00.190 --> 20:01.990
It can't be!

20:04.030 --> 20:07.830
All right, it appears your business here is done,
so I ask you leave.

20:07.830 --> 20:09.640
Um, we, uh...

20:09.640 --> 20:11.430
Oh, for crying out loud!

20:19.110 --> 20:19.750
There he is!

20:19.750 --> 20:21.210
Up there!
There he is!

20:39.270 --> 20:41.060
Who are you?

21:09.830 --> 21:11.800
It's you! No-Face!

21:21.280 --> 21:22.410
Damn...

21:22.410 --> 21:24.570
Where is he?! Where'd he go?

21:25.710 --> 21:27.840
Where the hell did he go?!

21:45.900 --> 21:47.470
Sorry to keep you waiting.

21:47.470 --> 21:50.340
Master Robès! You're all right then?

21:50.340 --> 21:52.670
Yeah, good work on your part too.

21:52.670 --> 21:56.010
Oh, thank goodness.

21:56.880 --> 22:00.280
I told you there's no way I'd be caught.

22:01.480 --> 22:03.280
Thank goodness...

22:03.950 --> 22:06.480
I'm so glad you're all right!

22:07.550 --> 22:09.180
Right...

22:10.020 --> 22:11.820
Who's there?!

22:16.130 --> 22:18.100
It can't be!

22:50.400 --> 22:54.270
I want to peak inside your heart, and find
out your feelings and expressions

22:54.270 --> 22:58.170
I see you bearing your burden alone, and don't
ask the reason for your twinkling tears

22:58.170 --> 23:01.740
I give you a shout of support without mentioning
them, between the answers I'm looking for

23:01.740 --> 23:05.870
Without obsessing or over thinking,
I feel sunbeams in the future you

23:07.580 --> 23:09.420
It feels nice, very, very much

23:09.420 --> 23:11.220
You and me, we're very, very good

23:11.220 --> 23:15.090
I'd like to be there for you any time

23:15.090 --> 23:16.920
Very, very much, whenever

23:16.920 --> 23:18.760
Very, very good, not changing

23:18.760 --> 23:24.720
We're always blooming full of hope,
with all our might (Oh)

23:30.240 --> 23:32.710
I feel this kindness amidst my doubt

23:34.010 --> 23:36.480
I will always have faith in you at all times

23:37.740 --> 23:41.650
Here in this vast landscape
under the sunny blue sky

23:41.650 --> 23:45.780
We got good feelings, good social standing,
we're good; I want to always be here

23:47.250 --> 23:49.060
It feels nice, very, very much

23:49.060 --> 23:50.890
You and me, we're very, very good

23:50.890 --> 23:54.690
I'd like to be there for you any time

23:54.690 --> 23:56.560
Very, very much, whenever

23:56.560 --> 23:58.430
Very, very good, not changing

23:58.430 --> 24:04.390
We're always blooming full of hope,
with all our might (Oh)

24:16.350 --> 24:19.950
Next Time
The Traitor’s Whereabouts

24:16.750 --> 24:19.950


Next time, "The Traitor's Whereabouts"
